# Dummy for Debian trixie's libgl1-mesa-dri: the real library is the mesa that rootfs/mesa/build-mesa.sh puts under /usr/local
# (panfrost only, Wayland platform, glvnd, no LLVM). Debian's own libgl1-mesa-dri would pull mesa-libgallium and libllvm19
# (187 MiB). rootfs/build-rootfs.sh builds this file into a .deb (dpkg-deb, the same fields equivs-build reads) and
# installs it with the base image, so apt knows the dependency is met.
# The epoch keeps every Debian mesa update (25.0.7-2+deb13uN) below this version: apt never swaps a dummy for the real
# package. Debian's dependencies on these packages are ">=" (kodi, wlroots, libegl1), except libglx-mesa0's exact
# one on mesa-libgallium - see libglx-mesa0.control.
Package: libgl1-mesa-dri
Version: 1:25.0.7-2+deb13u1
Architecture: arm64
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: libgbm1 (= 1:25.0.7-2+deb13u1)
Description: dummy for libgl1-mesa-dri (h713 mesa under /usr/local)
 No files. The library comes from the mesa build in /usr/local/lib, which
 only this image's own build provides; see rootfs/mesa/build-mesa.sh.
